  "query_preview": "..(Thursday through Monday) \nIssued at 425 AM EST TUE NOV 3 2026\n\nBehind the shortwave trough and a cold front departing to the \neast, drier air will spread across the remainder of eastern KY on \nThursday. This will result in a trend to drier weather as a trough\nbegins to take shape over sections of the Central to eastern \nConus. The upper low that will have reached the Great Lakes is \nprogged to weaken to an open wave as it moves into Canada and a \n500 mb shortwave trough axis should trek across the Great Lakes \nand near the Lower OH Valley by late Thursday night or Friday. \nAnother upper low may develop in the Great Lakes vicinity and \ntrack into the Northeast/St Lawrence Valley to begin the weekend, \nwhile the 500 mb shortwave trough axis moves across the OH Valley \nand eastern KY area later Friday into early on Saturday. Another \nsfc cold front associated with trough will cross eastern KY at \nthat point. Guidance generally has an increase in low and mid \nlevel rh with this boundary but moisture will be quite limited \nthis far to the south. Isolated showers producing light rainfall \ncannot be ruled out. Yet another upper low/shortwave trough may \nmove into eastern Canada to eastern Conus troughing to end the \nweekend and pass north of the OH Valley and send another cold \nfront across eastern KY. \n\nWith upper level troughing moving across the eastern Conus this\nweekend, before shifting east of the OH Valley and eastern KY \nearly next week, northwest flow aloft will be present. A trend to \nnear normal if not a bit below normal temperatures is anticipated.\nHighs are forecast to reach the upper 50s to lower 60s this \nweekend, before temperatures trend colder for Sunday night and \nMonday behind the second cold front as sfc high pressure builds \nin. Lows could near the freezing mark or possibly fall below \nfreezing for several valley locations and low lying areas over \nthe weekend or early next week.",
